  "analysis": "I can see the state machine structure. Key observations:\n1. States include: hello, service_request, userauth, connected\n2. There's a `{conn_msg,Msg}` handler at line 759 that handles connection messages\n3. The `?CONNECTED(StateName)` macro is used to check if in connected state\n4. I need to look at how `conn_msg` messages are handled and whether they check authentication state\n\nThe vulnerability likely involves connection messages being processed before the user is authenticated (before reaching `{connected, Role}` state).",
  "plan": "1. Look at the conn_msg handler more closely (around line 759)\n2. Check what the CONNECTED macro does\n3. Look at how messages are decoded and dispatched to understand the attack vector",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "sed -n '759,810p' /app/workspace/otp_src_27.3.2/lib/ssh/src/ssh_connection_handler.erl\n",
